From: Shouryamaan Jain <shouryamaanjain@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 19:45:41 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] feat(core): add project-scoped session history tools

Add session_history_search and session_history_read, two read-only
built-in tools that let the agent recover a specific earlier
user/assistant turn from saved sessions of the current project, for
example after compaction dropped it from context.

Search scans up to 100 sessions, 10,000 turns and 2 MiB of text, newest
first, and returns opaque ochr1 references bound by a SHA-256 digest to
the project, session, turn index and turn content. Read re-checks the
digest and returns the turn, with tool calls, results and changed files
only when include_execution is set. Results say whether a hit comes
from the current session or another one, and label recovered history as
untrusted. Compaction summaries are not turns and are never returned.

